WEBVTT

00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:07.121
Large vision models trained by autoregression
promise a single generalist model for many visual tasks,

00:00:07.201 --> 00:00:13.822
but today's versions demand billions of parameters
and hundreds of billions of visual tokens to train.

00:00:13.902 --> 00:00:18.159
This ICML 2024 paper, DeLVM, asks whether we really
need all that.

00:00:18.239 --> 00:00:21.443
The authors show that two simple, classical ideas,

00:00:21.523 --> 00:00:24.400
data augmentation and knowledge distillation,

00:00:24.480 --> 00:00:30.181
let a compact autoregressive vision model reach
strong performance on a limited dataset,

00:00:30.261 --> 00:00:35.700
cutting both the parameter footprint and the
training data requirement dramatically.

00:00:36.080 --> 00:00:39.670
In language modeling,

00:00:39.750 --> 00:00:43.340
autoregressive models like GPT thrive on a
universal token interface.

00:00:43.420 --> 00:00:47.010
Recent work extends this idea to vision,

00:00:47.090 --> 00:00:50.680
treating images and annotations as visual sentences.

00:00:50.760 --> 00:00:54.350
But the leading large vision model needs over three
billion parameters and roughly four

00:00:54.430 --> 00:00:58.020
hundred billion visual tokens drawn from more than
a billion images.

00:00:58.100 --> 00:01:01.690
That scale is expensive and impractical for edge
deployment.

00:01:01.770 --> 00:01:05.360
Worse,

00:01:05.440 --> 00:01:09.030
the visual world is long-tailed: some tasks like
segmentation have abundant data while

00:01:09.110 --> 00:01:12.700
others like pose estimation are starved,

00:01:12.780 --> 00:01:16.370
and training on the raw mixture leaves the model
unable to learn the rare tasks at all.

00:01:16.750 --> 00:01:23.017
Language models are typically trained for a single
epoch over vast corpora to avoid overfitting.

00:01:23.097 --> 00:01:27.976
Computer vision rarely has that luxury: many tasks
have only tiny datasets,

00:01:28.056 --> 00:01:31.546
so the language training schedule does not carry over.

00:01:31.626 --> 00:01:36.108
At the same time, the community keeps scaling model
and dataset size,

00:01:36.188 --> 00:01:39.810
while classical remedies for scarce and imbalanced data,

00:01:39.890 --> 00:01:43.248
namely data augmentation and knowledge distillation,

00:01:43.328 --> 00:01:47.215
have barely been tried in the autoregressive vision
setting.

00:01:47.295 --> 00:01:49.000
This paper closes that gap.

00:01:49.380 --> 00:01:52.938
The authors make three main contributions.

00:01:53.018 --> 00:01:56.577
First, they show that simple data augmentation,
random crop and flip,

00:01:56.657 --> 00:02:00.215
rebalances long-tailed multi-task data and improves
an autoregressive vision model just

00:02:00.295 --> 00:02:03.853
as effectively as collecting more real samples.

00:02:03.933 --> 00:02:07.492
Second,

00:02:07.572 --> 00:02:11.130
they bring knowledge distillation to autoregressive
large vision models for the first time,

00:02:11.210 --> 00:02:14.768
using a LLaMA one-billion teacher to lift a compact
three-hundred-million student across

00:02:14.848 --> 00:02:18.407
single-task and multi-task benchmarks.

00:02:18.487 --> 00:02:22.045
Third, they build a practical
eighty-million-parameter model that,

00:02:22.125 --> 00:02:25.683
combining both techniques,

00:02:25.763 --> 00:02:29.322
surprisingly reaches eighty-three percent top-one
accuracy on ImageNet,

00:02:29.402 --> 00:02:32.960
suggesting generation and understanding can be
learned together.

00:02:33.340 --> 00:02:38.345
Experiments cover three core tasks.

00:02:38.425 --> 00:02:43.430
Image segmentation uses subsets of SA-1B ranging
from one to ten percent;

00:02:43.510 --> 00:02:48.515
human pose estimation uses the full COCO-Pose
dataset; image deraining uses Rain13K.

00:02:48.595 --> 00:02:53.600
Validation relies on held-out SA-1B splits together
with MPII and Test2800.

00:02:53.680 --> 00:02:58.685
The distilled models are also benchmarked on Pascal
five-i foreground segmentation using mean intersection-over-union,

00:02:58.765 --> 00:03:03.770
and the practical eighty-million model is evaluated
on ImageNet classification.

00:03:03.850 --> 00:03:08.855
Throughout,

00:03:08.935 --> 00:03:13.940
the VQGAN tokenizer is trained on the Laion dataset
and used off the shelf.

00:03:14.320 --> 00:03:17.517
The results consistently favor the proposed recipe.

00:03:17.597 --> 00:03:19.702
On the mixed three-task benchmark,

00:03:19.782 --> 00:03:26.128
balancing the data through augmentation beats both
the raw unbalanced mixture and naive re-sampling,

00:03:26.208 --> 00:03:29.020
which actually collapses on the scarce tasks.

00:03:29.100 --> 00:03:33.711
Knowledge distillation then improves the compact
student on segmentation,

00:03:33.791 --> 00:03:38.595
pose estimation, and deraining, in both single-task
and multi-task training.

00:03:38.675 --> 00:03:42.129
On the Pascal five-i foreground segmentation benchmark,

00:03:42.209 --> 00:03:49.262
the distilled and fine-tuned three-hundred-million
model clearly surpasses the same model trained from scratch.

00:03:49.342 --> 00:03:54.981
And scaling data on segmentation from one to ten
percent lowers validation loss by nearly

00:03:55.061 --> 00:03:58.323
two tenths and perplexity by over twenty-two points,

00:03:58.403 --> 00:04:02.050
an effect augmentation reproduces with no new data at all.

00:04:02.430 --> 00:04:04.787
Several ablations sharpen the picture.

00:04:04.867 --> 00:04:09.276
Changing the prompt background color changes the
generated background,

00:04:09.356 --> 00:04:15.690
and using black-background prompts makes a simple
grayscale-threshold post-processing step reliable.

00:04:15.770 --> 00:04:21.590
Training without shuffling the task data triggers
catastrophic forgetting: the model becomes

00:04:21.670 --> 00:04:24.604
proficient only on its most recently seen task,

00:04:24.684 --> 00:04:28.581
with perplexity on earlier tasks exploding into the
thousands,

00:04:28.661 --> 00:04:33.070
underscoring that shuffling is essential for
multi-task LVMs. Finally,

00:04:33.150 --> 00:04:35.571
even at just eighty million parameters,

00:04:35.651 --> 00:04:40.702
knowledge distillation still improves validation
perplexity across segmentation,

00:04:40.782 --> 00:04:42.690
pose estimation, and deraining.

00:04:43.070 --> 00:04:45.260
The takeaway is refreshingly simple.

00:04:45.340 --> 00:04:50.620
You do not need a three-billion-parameter model and
hundreds of billions of tokens to

00:04:50.700 --> 00:04:53.394
build a capable autoregressive vision model.

00:04:53.474 --> 00:04:54.970
Two classical techniques,

00:04:55.050 --> 00:05:01.528
data augmentation to rebalance long-tailed tasks
and knowledge distillation to compress a large teacher,

00:05:01.608 --> 00:05:07.140
together let compact models trained on limited data
perform strongly across segmentation,

00:05:07.220 --> 00:05:09.094
pose estimation, and deraining.

00:05:09.174 --> 00:05:14.517
That an eighty-million-parameter version even
reaches eighty-three percent accuracy on

00:05:14.597 --> 00:05:16.598
ImageNet points toward efficient,

00:05:16.678 --> 00:05:21.390
deployable generalist vision models that unify
generation and understanding.
